WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.964
Thread one reads index eight from the

00:00:02.964 --> 00:00:05.076
index array, then fetches value one

00:00:05.076 --> 00:00:06.836
hundred eight from that position.

00:00:11.336 --> 00:00:13.919
The indices are eight elements apart. How

00:00:13.919 --> 00:00:16.132
many aligned thirty-two byte sectors do

00:00:16.132 --> 00:00:17.608
their value reads touch?

00:00:26.108 --> 00:00:29.240
Each value lies in a different sector. The

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.588
eight consecutive index reads touch one

00:00:31.588 --> 00:00:33.546
sector, under the same alignment

00:00:33.546 --> 00:00:33.937
assumption.
